        "title": "Expert Backed Review Summary",
        "text": "<p>Shameless Snacks takes familiar sour gummy candy and reformulates it for shoppers who want to cut back on sugar without completely giving up candy. The assortment includes fruity options such as <strong>peach, watermelon, red raspberry, blue raspberry, and green apple</strong>, giving the pack enough variety for people who prefer switching between different sweet-and-sour flavors. The biggest nutritional difference compared with conventional gummies is the sugar and fiber content. A 50g serving contains <strong>70 calories, 3g of total sugar, no added sugar, and 26g of dietary fiber</strong>. The formula relies heavily on polydextrose and soluble corn fiber, along with erythritol, isomalt, and sucralose for sweetness. The gummies are also made with <strong>pectin rather than gelatin</strong>, making them suitable for vegan diets. Product listings additionally identify them as gluten-free and keto-friendly. Colors come from ingredients including vegetable juice concentrate, beta-carotene, spirulina extract, and spinach powder rather than conventional artificial dyes. </p>",
